# CardSage Cursor Rules (.cursorrules)
# Applicable to all Flutter/Dart development in this workspace

[General]
language = "dart"
framework = "flutter"
architecture = "clean_architecture"
state_management = "provider_and_value_notifier"

[Architecture Rules]
- Adhere strictly to Feature-First Clean Architecture: core/ and features/<feature>/(domain, data, presentation).
- Presentation layer: ZERO setState(). Calling setState() is strictly forbidden.
- Use ChangeNotifier with Provider for application/feature state machines (ViewState: initial, loading, loaded, empty, error, refreshing).
- Use ValueNotifier<T> and ValueListenableBuilder<T> for local widget state (tab selection, input mask, card flip, modal sheets).
- All screens must extend StatelessWidget.
- Keep widget build methods clean and decompose large trees into focused, const-friendly leaf widgets.

[Code Quality & MNC Standards]
- Always apply 'const' constructors wherever possible to maximize render performance.
- Never write inline Color(0x...) or hardcoded hex colors in widgets; use AppColors.*.
- Never use arbitrary icon libraries or raw icons in screens; use centralized AppIcons.* in core/constants/app_icons.dart.
- Typography must reference AppTypography.* or Theme.of(context).textTheme.
- Padding and spacing must reference AppDimensions.*.
- Handle every edge case: offline status, 401 unauthorized, 404 not found, 500 server errors, empty data lists.
- Provide comprehensive docstrings and comments on public methods.

[Security & Zero-Knowledge Vault]
- Full 16-digit PANs and CVVs are strictly local-only and stored in SecureVaultService (hardware-backed flutter_secure_storage).
- Never transmit raw card numbers or CVV to the backend API.
- Prompt biometric authentication (local_auth) before revealing or copying PAN/CVV.
- Implement 30-second auto-clear timer on clipboard operations.
